                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Finally, I finished the story. I had a mixed feelings, so I had to decide where to put my vote. Then I just see, that Atom RPG 2 just changed his hall genre shortly after closing kickstarter backing. That's very not cool.\nBecause every review is about comparing to Fallout 1-2, I have to do the same. Many positive reviews are just defending this game based off this is an indie game, and Fallout is legend. Guys! Black Isle Studios first two games were the Fallout 1-2, they were just starters as well.\nSo quick compare. \nFallout has better story, Atom RPG stroy is kinda go to the bunker (known from the very start) -> go to the main hub -> go to two exact location -> come back and showdown. (however the idea behind the story is ok)\nFallout has better quest design. Atom RPG made many questioable choices, like hiding the hall Factory questline behind a mushroom gather quest, making quest trigger points in some non-logical way so you can sometimes lock yourself out from a quest if you use the open map you wanted, not how they imagined.. Sometimes the journal does not mention who was the questgiver, so I had to google it if I wanted to report its finished. NPCs usually like Pillars of Eternity fan made NPCs, with no real reason to talk to them. You don't have to force an dialog window for NPCs which has nothing interesting to say (if i click on them saying some oneliners would have been more practical). \nMy \"favourite\" that you can exhaust options with NPCs. When I talked to a guard on a ship he did not let me see his boss. After I got a quest to visit him, I couldn't because the option was already exhausted before. Other way to locked out of quests.\nFallout has better setting. I don't think this needs explanation. Here we have a post nuclear post soviet enviroment, where we not just using drugs (like americans in Fallout), alcohol is a solution for many problem.\nThe character creation was kinda 1-1 stolen from Fallout, but somehow any attempt to make it different, made it worse.\nCompanions are better in Fallout and more easy to find. Without wiki, I guess I would have only Fidel, which would have been suicide, considering how difficult the fight can be. (however later I used the timed bomb drop tactic in every major main story fight...just works)\nAtom RPG looks better. If you crave for more postnuclear RPG and you have exhausted all other options in \"A\" category, you can try. Maybe it will work better for you. For me, as I started it was mixed experince with some value in it, but after almost 10 year support and still has some very incomplete or flawed development solution.\nAtom RPG 2 looks even worse.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1793667836,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1793667836,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 5,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.5573645830154419,
                        "comment_count": 1,
                        "steam_purchase": false,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Greetings! You talking yourself out of an important quest-related dialogue option sounds like a bug, we will check it ASAP. ATOM RPG is not really competing with classic Fallout, one of our favorite games, we just wanted to make our own story taking inspiration from what we love. A real shame that comparing our game with a cult classic we never really wished to \"compete\" with was the basis for the negative review, but still, thank you for the support!",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1793910004,
